{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Mount Sinai smoked in its entirety.</b> It was the mountain that smoked, and not the fire — for the fire that is before the glory of YHWH has no smoke. And what it says, 'like the smoke of a furnace' — it is known that the likeness is not like the thing likened; but because we are corporeal beings, it is impossible for us to arrange and liken the intelligible matters except through the corporeal things in which we are immersed. And so too Scripture likened the beauty of the sun and its radiance to the beauty of a human being, and its course in its sphere to the course of the mighty warrior — as it is written (Psalms 19:6): ״והוא כחתן יוצא מחפתו ישיש כגבור לרוץ אורח״, and it is a well-known thing that it is not on its level and does not resemble it one bit in a thousand thousands and myriads of myriads of times. And so too Scripture likened the Holy One, blessed be He, to a lion, as it is said (Amos 3:8): ״אריה שאג מי לא יירא ה' אלהים דבר מי לא ינבא״ — the reason being that there is among all corporeal living creatures none mightier than it, and so as to accommodate the ear to what it is able to hear; and concerning things such as this, the Rabbis, blessed be their memory, said: the Torah spoke in the language of human beings."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:10.464341455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}